      "notes_md": "From 2026: It was a student that introduced me to this film as I was teaching the Moviegoer's Guide to the Future course at ASU, which is based on the book Films from the Future. I was absolutely captivated by the story telling and the twist. This would probably make the cut for a sequel to the book given the way it explores complex issues - especially around what it means to be human. During COVID I was working on a parallel course on infectious disease-based movies with a friend that we never ended up teaching. This movie was on the list. It also opens up the whole field of fungi and human impacts which to this day remains underexplored. Claude: Takes Never Let Me Go's \"what do we owe engineered beings?\" question and pushes it one step further — what if the engineered being is also the species' successor? Shares thematic DNA with Splice and belongs alongside the brain-organoid moral-status discussion.\n\n---",
