      "notes_md": "From 2026: Looking back I'm not sure why this didn't make the top 50 shortlist for the bok. Possibly because while it's a lot of fun and has a lot of memorable moments/themes, it's harder to draw out conersations from these. Or possibly because I forgot! Claude: Another Philip K. Dick adaptation — a man discovers his memories may have been implanted, and his identity may be a corporate fabrication. The original is gloriously over the top; the remake plays it straighter. Both explore territory that connects to Ghost in the Shell's identity questions and Eternal Sunshine's memory themes. What are you when your memories aren't real?\n\n---",
      "andrew_response_md": "",
      "summary": "In 2084 a construction worker bored with his life buys a memory implant for the Mars vacation he can't afford. The procedure unlocks a buried second identity and a real-world conspiracy."
